1.text:
With  $P_{0}=0$ and $X_{i}=T_{i}e_{K_{i}},\;T_{i}\sim U(-1,1)$,
$K_{i}\sim{\rm Unif}\{1,\dots ,n\}$ i.i.d. the $n$–simplex
$[0,X_{1}\dots X_{n}]$ is non degenerate iff $K_{1},\dots ,K_{n}$ is a
permutation.  On a permutation

${\rm Vol}_{n}=n!^{-1}\bigl|\det[X_{1}\dots X_{n}]\bigr|
      =n!^{-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}|T_{i}|$, 
${\mathbb P}\{K\;{\rm perm}\}=n!/n^{n}$ and ${\mathbb E}|T|=1/2$ so that
with the usual $n!$–volume

\begin{equation*}
{\mathbb E}{\rm Vol}_{n}
   =\frac{n!}{n^{n}}\frac1{n!}\Bigl(\frac12\Bigr)^{n}=(2n)^{-n},
 \qquad {\mathbb E}{\rm Vol}_{1}=1/2,
\end{equation*}
and ${\rm Vol}_{n}=0$ on a collision.  Put
$a={\mathbb E}|T_{1}-T_{2}|=2/3$ and

\begin{equation*}
b={\mathbb E}\sqrt{T_{1}^{2}+T_{2}^{2}}
  =\iint_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}du\,dv
  =\frac{\sqrt2+\ln(1+\sqrt2)}{3}=0.765195716\ldots
\end{equation*}
For two i.i.d. copies

${\mathbb E}\|X-Y\|=n^{-1}a+(n-1)n^{-1}b=:D_{n}$.
For the $N=n+1$ points $\{0,X_{i}\}$

\begin{equation*}
\bar D_{n}
 =\frac{n{\mathbb E}|X|+\binom n2D_{n}}{\binom{N}{2}}
 =\frac{1+(n-1)D_{n}}{n+1}
 =\frac{n+(n-1)a+(n-1)^{2}b}{n(n+1)},\qquad 
\bar D_{1}=1/2,
\end{equation*}
$\bar D_{n}\to b$.  Hence on the i.i.d. cross

\begin{equation*}
R_{n}:=\frac{{\mathbb E}{\rm Vol}_{n}}{\bar D_{n}}
 =\frac{(n+1)(2n)^{-n}}{1+(n-1)D_{n}}
 =\frac{n(n+1)(2n)^{-n}}
        {\,n+(n-1)a+(n-1)^{2}b\,},\qquad R_{1}=1,
\end{equation*}
$R_{n}=O\!\left((2n)^{-n}\right)$.

In particular

* $R_{1}=1.000000$,
* $R_{2}=1.125/(8+3b)=0.109270\ldots$,
* $R_{3}=1/(78+72b)=0.007513\ldots$,
* $R_{4}=5/[1024(6+9b)]=3.79\times10^{-4}$,
* $R_{5}=1.51\times10^{-5}$, $R_{6}\approx4.9\times10^{-7}$.

The series is therefore exhausted at $n=3$.  With
$S_{N}=\sum_{n\ge1}R_{n}$

\begin{equation*}
S_{N}=1+0.109270+0.007513+0.000379+0.000015+\cdots
\end{equation*}
and

\begin{equation*}
S_{\infty}= \sum_{n\ge1}\frac{n(n+1)(2n)^{-n}}
            {\,n+(n-1)2/3+(n-1)^{2}b\,}
        =1.11717\ldots\approx1.117,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $S_{\infty}\approx1.117\!-\!1.118$ on the three figure scale.
The $n=1$ normalisation is $R_{1}=1$ and the non-trivial i.i.d.
contribution is

$\displaystyle\sum_{n\ge2}R_{n}=S_{\infty}-1\approx0.1172$, essentially
$R_{2}+R_{3}\approx0.11678$, the conventional one-point-per-axis,
collision free normalisation ${\mathbb E}{\rm Vol}_{n}=2^{-n}/n!$
giving the familiar $R_{n}^{\rm ax}=(n+1)2^{-n}/\{n![1+(n-1)b]\}$ and
$\sum_{n}R_{n}^{\rm ax}\approx1.2497\approx1.250$.  This is the
$n!/n^{n}$ occupancy corrected i.i.d. on the union $\bigcup_{k}[-1,1]e_{k}$
value quoted in the statement. ∎

